{"kind":"table","sheet":"Practice Guide","address":"A1:B16","rows":16,"cols":2,"values":[["Truck Inventory practice",""],["Data","All loads, POs, destinations, and quantities are fictional practice data."],["1. Upload","In Truck Inventory > Inputs, upload this file under Upload combined load sheet."],["2. Parse","Parse the input, then select PRACTICE-101 to start."],["3. Item Setup","Enter the sample dimensions and weights below for each selected load."],["4. Build","Select Dry Van and build the truck plan. Try the other loads and compare results."],["Quantity meaning","Qty is the number of physical units with the dimensions entered in Item Setup."],["Units","Dimensions are inches. Weight is pounds per unit."],["Sample Item Setup",""],["681943924","Full Pallet: Length 40, Width 48, Height 15.5, Weight 110. Stackable: No. Stack Qty: 1."],["683054545","Half Pallet: Length 20, Width 48, Height 52.7, Weight 350. Stackable: No. Stack Qty: 1."],["PRACTICE-101","24 units. Start here for a smaller mixed load."],["PRACTICE-102","40 units. Compare the larger mixed load with the first load."],["PRACTICE-103","68 units. Explore capacity handling and truck assignments."],["Optional exercise","Change stackability and Stack Qty in Item Setup and rebuild to compare results."],["Editing the file","Keep the FINAL LS column headers. Add or change data rows to create more scenarios."]]}
